drm/vgem: don't call drm_clflush_pages() on arm64

vgem_prime_pin() calls drm_clflush_pages() so importers can rely on a
coherent exported dma-address. That helper only flushes on x86 and
powerpc. On every other architecture, arm64 included, it just logs
"Architecture has no drm_cache.c support" and does nothing, so every
dma-buf export of a vgem object (each frame of a Zink/Wayland window)
spams the kernel log.

Skip the call there. On arm64 the cache maintenance for the importer is
done by dma_map_sg() on the device, which gets real DMA ops from
04.vgem_arm64_dma_ops.patch. n_pages becomes __maybe_unused for the
configurations that compile the call out.

This is the one hunk of Droidspaces-Mali patches/kernel/0002 (written for
the 5.15 GKI vgem) that applies to 4.19. Its other hunk, vma_set_file(),
is not needed: the 4.19 vgem already open codes the vm_file swap.

Independent of 04: the two patches touch different functions and apply in
either order.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/vgem/vgem_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/vgem/vgem_drv.c
index 8920770d1..9144a0d3c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vgem/vgem_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vgem/vgem_drv.c
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@ static void vgem_unpin_pages(struct drm_vgem_gem_object *bo)
 static int vgem_prime_pin(struct drm_gem_object *obj)
 {
 	struct drm_vgem_gem_object *bo = to_vgem_bo(obj);
-	long n_pages = obj->size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+	long n_pages __maybe_unused = obj->size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 	struct page **pages;
 
 	pages = vgem_pin_pages(bo);
@@ -296,8 +296,13 @@ static int vgem_prime_pin(struct drm_gem_object *obj)
 
 	/* Flush the object from the CPU cache so that importers can rely
 	 * on coherent indirect access via the exported dma-address.
+	 * drm_clflush_pages() only does that on x86 and powerpc; elsewhere
+	 * it just logs "Architecture has no drm_cache.c support" on every
+	 * pin. On arm64 the cache maintenance is done by dma_map_sg().
 	 */
+#if defined(CONFIG_X86) || defined(__powerpc__)
 	drm_clflush_pages(pages, n_pages);
+#endif
 
 	return 0;
 }
